Apple's Sign in with Apple logo

apple-logo-white.svg and apple-logo-black.svg are Apple's artwork, copied unmodified from
Apple's "Sign in with Apple - Logo Only" set (the white and black logo-only SVG files). They
are not covered by the Apache License that applies to the rest of this project. They may be used
only under Apple's Human Interface Guidelines and the Sign in with Apple terms; do not change
them.

The server serves them only while both files exist (build.rs turns on cfg(apple_logo)). A
self-hoster who does not want them can delete both files: the button is then text-only.
The test `the_logo_files_are_apples_originals_committed_in_the_repo` (crates/ibridge-hosted/src/
pages/assets_tests.rs) guards that this repository ships the files; delete it too when you delete
the files. `the_apple_logo_is_used_exactly_when_its_files_are_present` passes either way.
